<http://data.silknow.org/object/44b402db-8f34-30ac-a4e4-6ec97698bce6/observation/1>
        a                   crmsci:S4_Observation ;
        ecrm:P2_has_type    <http://data.silknow.org/observation/technical-observation> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note    "Dress fabric of woven silk, twill binding.\nBias cut fabric patterned with a series of two narrow stripes.\n[1] white ground with a dark grey meandering stem bearing leaves and alternate red and pale blue flower heads.\n[2] asymmetrically placed similar meander in grey with leaves and pink or blue flower heads.\nEach stripe is separated by a very narrow grey and white stripe.\nWarp: white, grey, pink silk.\nWeft: white, light blue, grey, red and pink silk.\n\nType possibly known as Hussein Kuli Khan."@en ;
        crmsci:O8_observed  <http://data.silknow.org/object/44b402db-8f34-30ac-a4e4-6ec97698bce6> .

